    "field": "Global biogeochemical cycles",
    "problem": "Current Earth system models inadequately represent how the nitrogen cycle interacts with and limits the carbon cycle, creating substantial uncertainty in projections of the biosphere's capacity to absorb anthropogenic CO\u2082 and thus in predicting future climate change.",
    "method": "To address uncertainties in climate change, the paper proposes adopting an Earth-system perspective that investigates the dynamics of the nitrogen cycle in the context of a changing carbon cycle, a changing climate, and changes in human actions.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze the interactions between the global nitrogen cycle, the carbon cycle, and climate, explaining how human-caused changes to nitrogen availability will affect the Earth system's capacity to absorb atmospheric carbon and regulate climate.",
